You can have that on Ubuntu:

# Ubuntu 16.04
sudo add-apt-repository ppa:ubuntugis/ubuntugis-unstable
sudo apt-get update

sudo apt-get install gdal-bin libgdal-dev libgeos-dev libproj-dev libudunits2-dev

Also for macOS (via brew <https://brew.sh/>):

brew tap osgeo/osgeos4mac
brew install gdal2-python
brew link --force gdal2-python

then in R:

install.packages(c("rgeos", "sp"), type = "source")
install.packages("rgdal", type = "source", configure.args = c("--with-proj-include=/usr/local/include", "--with-proj-lib=/usr/local/lib"))
install.packages("sf", type = "source")

Alex

